 widely recognized the way they should have been. And, and, um, and to call myself out on that,

00:27:14.290 --> 00:27:19.130
 you know, is really important for me and to live with that complexity and say, and I'm trying to do

00:27:19.130 --> 00:27:25.870
 better and I want to reach for more and to allow for this complexity is to do exactly what you're

00:27:25.870 --> 00:27:31.910
 saying, which is to subvert a system that wants to eradicate the complexity of relationships and say,

00:27:32.030 --> 00:27:39.240
 you're either this or this, you know, and I am willing to say, um, look instead of like the or,

00:27:39.380 --> 00:27:45.870
 like, let's work on looking at the end, you know, we are this and this, and how can we find that place

00:27:45.870 --> 00:27:46.630
 of commonality?

00:27:47.510 --> 00:27:54.550
 Yeah. And I think it, that really comes across that, you know, one solution is not going to work,

00:27:54.550 --> 00:28:01.210
 right? So sustainability or hope for the future or kind of whatever you want to call it is a deeply

